WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.830
A dog has fur.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.660
A chicken has feathers.

3
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.590
Neither looks much like you.

4
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.760
But inside your cells is a
protein called cytochrome c.

5
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.180
It works in aerobic respiration.

6
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.080
In humans, it's a chain
of 104 amino acids.

7
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.270
Dogs, chickens, even tuna, make their own.

8
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.720
So how can one protein from your cells show
you're closer to a dog than to a chicken?

9
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.040
In this mission, you'll see which
clues reveal that species are related:

10
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.500
anatomy, fossils, DNA and proteins.

11
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.440
Then you'll read real
data for this one protein,

12
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.490
from six animals, chimpanzee to tuna.

13
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: find out how one protein
can reveal who your closer relatives are.
